        "The model, verified:\n\n```tsx\n// page.tsx — a Server Component: fetch AT RENDER, no effects\nexport default async function ProductPage({ params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> }) {\n  const { id } = await params;\n\n  // WATERFALL (bad): 200ms + 200ms = 400ms — second waits for first\n  const product = await getProduct(id);\n  const reviews = await getReviews(id);\n\n  // PARALLEL (good): both fly at once\n  const [product, reviews] = await Promise.all([getProduct(id), getReviews(id)]);\n\n  return <Product product={product} reviews={reviews} />;\n}\n\n// STREAMING: the slow part renders behind its own Suspense\n// (loading.tsx does this for the whole segment — the same machinery)\nasync function Reviews({ id }: { id: string }) {\n  const reviews = await getReviews(id);         // slow query\n  return <List items={reviews} />;\n}\nexport default function Page() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <ProductShell />                            {/* instant — shell paints NOW */}\n      <Suspense fallback={<ReviewsSkeleton />}>\n        <Reviews id={id} />                       {/* streams when ready */}\n      </Suspense>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n\n// MUTATION: a Server Action + revalidation\nasync function addToCart(formData: FormData) {\n  'use server';\n  await db.cart.add(Object.fromEntries(formData));\n  revalidatePath('/cart');                        // cache entry invalid → refetch\n}\n```\n\nThe three pieces (the interview core):\n1. FETCH IN THE SERVER COMPONENT — data fetching is part of RENDER: the page function awaits its data before producing elements. No client-side loading flags, no JSON waterfalls over the wire — the client receives the rendered result. Next's fetch is special: request memoization de-dupes identical calls within one render pass, and the data cache persists across requests (tag it: fetch(url, { next: { tags: ['product'] } }) for surgical invalidation).\n2. PARALLELISM — the waterfall rule: independent requests must Promise.all; dependent ones MUST chain (you need the product id before reviews). The diagnostic: read your awaits top-to-bottom and ask 'does line 2 need line 1's result?' — no → parallelize.\n3. STREAMING + MUTATION — Suspense boundaries let slow data NOT block the shell; server actions close the loop (mutate → revalidate tag/path → the router refetches the affected server components → the UI updates with fresh data — no client cache to manage).",
